# skill-package-freshness gate — enforcement sentinel (#2656)
#
# This committed marker governs whether the .skill package content-freshness CI gate
# (`deploy.sh --check-package-freshness`, i.e. Check 7's content-hash verdict) BLOCKS
# or merely REPORTS when a rostered skill's compiled `.skill` package is stale versus
# its source (SKILL.md / references/). The probe reads this file directly, so the
# sentinel is load-bearing on its own; the thin CI workflow
# (skill-package-freshness.yml) additionally consumes the probe's exit code.
#
# The first non-comment, non-blank line is the mode token:
#   warn      → report only (exit-2, advisory); a STALE package is surfaced with a
#               true, non-zero exit code but does not block.
#   enforce   → block on a STALE package (exit-1 propagates to the CI caller).
#
# GRADUATED 2026-09-04: token flipped warn -> enforce.
# The stated precondition (">=3-day warn-log review with zero false positives") was judged
# UNSATISFIABLE rather than satisfied: the content arm had never executed in CI, so the
# accumulated warn log was the output of a probe that measured nothing. A positive
# falsification test is accepted as the substitute evidence, on this explicit sequencing:
# this flip FIRST, then a seeded stale package proved RED on the release branch WHILE this
# check is still non-required, then a byte-exact revert proved GREEN, then merge (operator
# decision D-6181Arm, Arm A conditioned). The proof FOLLOWS this commit and does not
# precede it — stating it here in the past tense would be the same declared-vs-actual
# defect this flip exists to close.
# Dep #2159 (non-reproducible-archive false positives) is CLOSED.
# The out-of-tree half — adding "Pre-merge .skill package content-freshness gate" to
# required_status_checks — is an operator step executed AFTER the release merges.
#
# (Token-flagged rather than presence-flagged so the file could ship ahead of the flip —
#  the docs referenced it while the gate was still non-blocking; mirrors
#  close-completeness.enforce.)
enforce
